### Discussed in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/discussions/12653

```py
    def test_comments_with_dropped_column(self, metadata, connection):
        Table(
            "tbl_with_comments",
            metadata,
            Column(
                "id", types.Integer, primary_key=True, comment="pk comment"
            ),
            Column("foobar", Integer, comment=f"comment_foobar"),
            Column("foo", Integer, comment=f"comment_foo"),
            Column(
                "bar",
                Integer,
                comment=f"comment_bar",
            ),
        )
        metadata.create_all(connection)
        insp = inspect(connection)
        eq_(
            {
                c["name"]: c["comment"]
                for c in insp.get_columns("tbl_with_comments")
            },
            {
                "id": "pk comment",
                "foobar": "comment_foobar",
                "foo": "comment_foo",
                "bar": "comment_bar",
            },
        )

        connection.exec_driver_sql(
            "ALTER TABLE [tbl_with_comments] DROP COLUMN [foobar]"
        )
        insp = inspect(connection)
        eq_(
            {
                c["name"]: c["comment"]
                for c in insp.get_columns("tbl_with_comments")
            },
            {
                "id": "pk comment",
                "foo": "comment_foo",
                "bar": "comment_bar",
            },
        )


```

context: 

> I read the source code of sqlalchemy and found that [this line](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/f2eda87a6b7f1534851da2d0370bd034d1791bfc/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/mssql/base.py#L3669) may be incorrect. That is, `sys.extended_properties.minor_id` is not always equal to `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS.ORDINAL_POSITION`.

> When there are columns in the middle of a table being deleted, the minor_id of other columns will not be modified, while the `ORDINAL_POSITION` in `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS` seems to be always continuous. When I query the system table `sys.columns`, the columns' minor_id of the table I found misplaced comments are not continuous. Take the example above, it's 1, 3 and 4. Here the mismatch happened.
